    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** stands as the unquestioned anchor of the Zurich Zebras lineup with a dominant 80.98 score. Facing a vulnerable 4.81 xERA matchup against Lowder, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from an elite combination of a favorable park and a slow opposing delivery that heavily enhances his stolen base potential\u2014the most critical variable in our 5x5 build. Joining him as high-ceiling plays are **Christian Yelich** (75.84) and **Yordan Alvarez** (70.25). **Christian Yelich** earns a massive boost from a +16% park factor and a favorable platoon matchup, while **Yordan Alvarez** maintains elite status despite the L/L disadvantage, primarily due to his massive 0.443 xwOBA, which helps mitigate the risks posed by P\u00e9rez. **Trea Turner** and **Junior Caminero** also project strongly, with both benefiting from their high spots in the batting order, providing the necessary stability to navigate this evening's rotations.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Carson Benge**, whose score of 35.11 placed him just shy of our 40-point floor. While **Carson Benge** possesses a solid base projection, the combination of facing an elite arm in S\u00e1nchez (2.95 xERA) and the negative impact of a same-handed platoon suppressed his efficiency below the threshold required to displace our starters. Conversely, we are playing it cautious with **Josh Smith** and **Kazuma Okamoto**; both draw the unenviable task of facing deGrom. Their scores have been heavily penalized by deGrom\u2019s 2.98 xERA, limiting them to the fringe of our starting requirements. While we are starting them, their output is highly volatile, and we must monitor early-game developments closely. As a reminder, **Colt Keith**, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** remain unavailable for today's action, ensuring we stay 